    {
      "turn": 1,
      "doctor_question": "Hello, welcome. What brings you in to see me today?",
      "targeted_symptom": "S021",
      "patient_response": "Well, what brings me here is... my talking gets all mixed up. Like, I try to explain things to people, you know? I try to tell them about the keys. The keys for the building where I clean, because there's this one set that always sticks in the mop closet door. And if you don't jiggle it just right, you're stuck. Reminds me of when I was in jail, honestly. The doors there, they have that heavy sound, that *clank*. But then I try to tell them about the prayer rug, because the pattern on it is so intricate, like a maze. A maze like a chessboard, really. The knights, they move in an L-shape, jumping over things. But when I try to explain all this, about the keys and the jail and the rug and the chess pieces... people just look at me. They tell me they cannot follow what I am saying. They say I'm not making sense.",
