    {
      "turn": 2,
      "doctor_question": "How long have you noticed your thoughts and speech getting mixed up like this?",
      "targeted_symptom": "duration",
      "patient_response": "Well, let me think... how long. It's been about two years and five months, I'd say. Yeah, it started right after that brief detention... just a big misunderstanding at the building, really. They didn't have to make a big deal out of it, but they did. But that building, you know, the floors in the main lobby are terrazzo. It's a beautiful stone if you buff it right, but management buys this cheap wax now. Smells like fake lemons and ammonia. I can't stand the smell of lemons anymore. It reminds me of this bag of lemons I bought at the corner store once, and when I cut them open, they were just completely dry inside. Just hollow white pith. Pith... like those helmets, you know? The ones the explorers wear in the old jungle movies. I saw a movie on Tuesday where this guy was running through the vines, swinging from trees, and his hat never fell off. Not even once. I don't know how they film that without the hat falling.",
