    {
      "turn": 4,
      "doctor_question": "Does your thinking and speech get mixed up even during times when you feel your energy is completely normal?",
      "targeted_symptom": "additional_requirement_3",
      "patient_response": "Well, normal energy... yeah, I guess so. There are weeks, you know, calmer weeks. Where I'm not buzzing out of my skin, and I'm not dragging on the floor either. Just... normal, I suppose. But even then, even when I feel fine for like, more than two weeks straight... I still hear him. The man in the vents. He just keeps talking. And I know the people in the building are still signaling each other about me. I can tell by how they look. \n\nLooking... you know, I used to look at the vents a lot when I was a kid. We lived in this apartment with these big metal grates, and they would rattle whenever the heat kicked on. It sounded like a train coming through the wall. I always loved trains. The way the wheels click-clack on the tracks, it's a rhythm. Like music. I bought a harmonica once, thought I could play the blues like they do on the trains, but I just couldn't get the breathing right. You have to breathe in and out so fast. Like a dog panting in the summer. Summer gets so hot here, the asphalt just melts right onto your shoes. Ruins the soles. I had to throw away a perfectly good pair of loafers because the tar just wouldn't come off...",
