    {
      "turn": 5,
      "doctor_question": "Looking back over these past two and a half years, would you say these periods of very high or very low energy have taken up most of that time?",
      "targeted_symptom": "additional_requirement_2",
      "patient_response": "Yeah, most of the time... most of the time since all this started, I've been in those keyed-up stretches. It's like I can't stop talking, and I take on these impossible cleaning plans, like scrubbing all the baseboards in the whole building with a toothbrush, and I just feel driven, you know? Like I absolutely cannot slow down. \n\nSlowing down... that reminds me of this old car my uncle used to have. It was a Buick, one of those massive ones from the seventies, painted this awful split-pea green color. He called it the Green Monster. The brakes on that thing were completely shot, so slowing down was always an adventure. We'd be coming up to a stop sign, and he'd just start pumping the pedal and praying. He kept a St. Christopher medal on the dashboard for luck. St. Christopher, the patron saint of travelers. My grandmother had a whole collection of saint medals in this little wooden box. The box smelled like cedar and old perfume, that powdery kind that sticks in the back of your throat. I swallowed a bug once when I was riding my bike, just flew right into my mouth...",
